{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For the tribe of Joseph, for the tribe of Manasseh.</b> Above he mentioned the tribe of Ephraim, for he gave precedence to Ephraim over Manasseh because of his rank. And the reason Scripture mentioned Joseph here among the spies is that he too brought an evil report, as it says (Genesis 37:2): ״ויבא יוסף את דבתם רעה״, and therefore Scripture mentioned him together with them and mentioned him together with Manasseh, for Gaddi son of Susi was among those who brought the evil report, but the tribe of Ephraim was delivered from this. And the reason Caleb and Joshua were not mentioned one after the other is so that Caleb would be surrounded by the spies before him and behind him, for so it was in his mouth with them; and do not say that the matter was the same with Joshua — therefore Scripture mentioned him afterward on his own, for he was not counted among them."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:57.700291577Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}